1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:15,000
残酷な天使のように 少年よ 神話になれ

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:38,000
青い風が今 胸のドアを叩いても 私だけをただ見つめて 微笑んでるあなた

3
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:45,000
そっと触れるもの 求めることに夢中で

4
00:00:45,000 --> 00:00:52,000
運命さえまだ知らない 痛い気な瞳

5
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:59,000
だけどいつか気づくでしょう その背中には

6
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:07,000
遥か未来 目指すための羽があること

7
00:01:07,000 --> 00:01:14,000
残酷な天使の帝世 窓辺からやがて到達

8
00:01:14,000 --> 00:01:22,000
もっと走る熱いパッドスで 思い出を裏切るなら

9
00:01:22,000 --> 00:01:30,000
この空を抱いて輝く 少年よ 神話になれ

10
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:31,000
次回予告

11
00:01:31,000 --> 00:01:33,000
次回予告

12
00:01:33,000 --> 00:01:34,000
次回予告

13
00:01:34,000 --> 00:01:36,000
次回予告

14
00:01:36,000 --> 00:01:37,000
次回予告

15
00:01:37,000 --> 00:01:38,000
次回予告

16
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:39,000
次回予告

17
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:41,000
次回予告

18
00:01:41,000 --> 00:01:43,000
次回予告

19
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:44,000
次回予告

20
00:01:44,000 --> 00:01:48,000
次回予告

21
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:49,000
次回予告

22
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:50,140
Oh, come on, Kaji.

23
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:53,040
This is what all the girls are wearing.

24
00:01:54,960 --> 00:01:55,840
Oh, really?

25
00:01:56,140 --> 00:01:56,560
Uh-huh.

26
00:01:56,840 --> 00:01:59,020
Oh, I'm so anxious about this school trip.

27
00:01:59,180 --> 00:02:00,740
I just know we'll have a great time.

28
00:02:01,040 --> 00:02:02,780
So, where is your class going?

29
00:02:03,540 --> 00:02:04,020
Okinawa!

30
00:02:04,560 --> 00:02:05,960
It's gonna be awesome.

31
00:02:06,360 --> 00:02:08,120
We're even gonna go scuba diving.

32
00:02:08,420 --> 00:02:09,520
Scuba diving, huh?

33
00:02:10,000 --> 00:02:13,060
Boy, it's been years since the last time I went diving.

34
00:02:13,300 --> 00:02:16,260
Hey, where'd you go for your school trip, Kaji?

35
00:02:16,260 --> 00:02:19,060
Well, actually, we didn't have one.

36
00:02:19,440 --> 00:02:20,720
Why is that?

37
00:02:21,000 --> 00:02:23,440
Just a little thing called the second impact.

38
00:02:30,040 --> 00:02:30,640
What?

39
00:02:31,300 --> 00:02:33,440
Did you just think I can't go on the trip?

40
00:02:34,580 --> 00:02:35,140
Yep.

41
00:02:35,640 --> 00:02:36,540
Well, why not?

42
00:02:36,800 --> 00:02:38,020
It's part of your job.

43
00:02:38,100 --> 00:02:39,500
You mean I'm on permanent standby?

44
00:02:39,980 --> 00:02:40,700
You got it.

45
00:02:40,740 --> 00:02:42,340
What idiot decided that?

46
00:02:42,460 --> 00:02:44,440
This one, the operations planning manager.

47
00:02:46,260 --> 00:02:46,760
Hmph.

48
00:02:49,100 --> 00:02:53,820
Shinji, why don't you stop hiding behind that cup of tea and talk some sense into this woman?

49
00:02:53,940 --> 00:02:54,940
Act like a man!

50
00:02:55,080 --> 00:02:59,000
Well, you know, actually, I had kind of expected that we wouldn't be allowed to go.

51
00:02:59,200 --> 00:03:00,700
So, you've already given up.

52
00:03:00,900 --> 00:03:01,280
Mm-hmm.

53
00:03:02,180 --> 00:03:03,380
Huh, pathetic.

54
00:03:03,640 --> 00:03:06,360
There's nothing more useless than a housebroken male.

55
00:03:06,600 --> 00:03:08,420
Hey, don't talk about me like that.

56
00:03:08,600 --> 00:03:09,040
Look!

57
00:03:09,240 --> 00:03:09,440
Hm?

58
00:03:09,440 --> 00:03:12,260
I know how you must feel, but there's just no other way.

59
00:03:12,620 --> 00:03:15,980
There's always the possibility that an angel might attack while you're away.

60
00:03:16,320 --> 00:03:19,840
So I get stuck here on standby status while everyone else is having fun?

61
00:03:20,000 --> 00:03:23,580
Why is it that we're the ones who always have to be ready to defend against them?

62
00:03:23,740 --> 00:03:26,600
Any good officer knows that the best defense is a good offense.

63
00:03:26,600 --> 00:03:29,080
Why can't we find them and attack them first?

64
00:03:29,600 --> 00:03:31,780
If we could do that, we would do it.

65
00:03:32,460 --> 00:03:36,320
Look, think of this as an opportunity to get ahead for a change.

66
00:03:36,620 --> 00:03:40,540
The two of you can catch up on your studies while the rest of your classmates are on the trip.

67
00:03:40,840 --> 00:03:43,280
Or did you think I hadn't seen these report cards?

68
00:03:43,280 --> 00:03:47,120
I guess you thought I wouldn't know about your test scores yet.

69
00:03:47,540 --> 00:03:50,260
Well, all of your grades are forwarded directly to my terminal,

70
00:03:50,560 --> 00:03:53,060
and I have been very disappointed with the both of you.

71
00:03:53,100 --> 00:03:56,540
Ha, this is so silly, and this school's grades are just dumb.

72
00:03:56,900 --> 00:04:00,560
The old-fashioned numeric grading scale you use on your exams is stupid.

73
00:04:00,940 --> 00:04:02,560
In Rome, do as the Romans do.

74
00:04:03,020 --> 00:04:05,620
You could at least try to adjust to Japanese school life.

75
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:08,220
This sucks!

76
00:04:08,220 --> 00:04:14,340
Hey, Asuka, I'll bring you back something nice!

77
00:04:14,760 --> 00:04:17,340
Ha, ha! Sayonara, suckers!

78
00:04:17,420 --> 00:04:20,160
Hey, don't worry. I'll have enough fun for the both of you!

79
00:04:20,160 --> 00:04:21,300
Ha, ha, ha, ha!

80
00:04:25,420 --> 00:04:30,160
Post the survey data on Mount Asuma from Balthazar to Melchior as soon as possible.

81
00:04:38,220 --> 00:04:42,640
A school trip, huh? That sounds pretty reckless in times like these.

82
00:04:42,980 --> 00:04:47,460
I guess the idea is to let all the kids have time to get out and act like kids while they can.

83
00:04:55,460 --> 00:04:57,520
Hmm, what have you got there, Shinji?

84
00:04:58,040 --> 00:04:59,280
Basic physics primer.

85
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:01,740
Oh, you're such an obedient student.

86
00:05:02,060 --> 00:05:05,260
Well, I'll have to study it anyway. I mean, I...

87
00:05:05,260 --> 00:05:10,660
Well, if I can't go diving in Okinawa, let's do it here.

88
00:05:11,120 --> 00:05:12,000
Do what?

89
00:05:12,260 --> 00:05:13,280
Diving, of course.

90
00:05:13,680 --> 00:05:15,140
So what are you working on?

91
00:05:15,400 --> 00:05:16,200
Let's see.

92
00:05:16,680 --> 00:05:19,160
You can't solve an easy problem like this?

93
00:05:20,220 --> 00:05:21,360
There, all done.

94
00:05:21,740 --> 00:05:23,360
It's easy when you know how.

95
00:05:23,740 --> 00:05:27,820
How can you solve a difficult problem like this and not make good grades on your tests?

96
00:05:28,480 --> 00:05:32,180
It's because I'm having too much trouble figuring out what the questions are.

97
00:05:32,460 --> 00:05:34,760
You mean you can't read the questions in Japanese?

98
00:05:35,180 --> 00:05:38,280
That's right. I still haven't learned all of the kanji yet.

99
00:05:38,600 --> 00:05:40,580
I didn't have to study it in college.

100
00:05:41,060 --> 00:05:41,940
You went to college?

101
00:05:42,380 --> 00:05:44,640
Yeah. I graduated last year.

102
00:05:45,420 --> 00:05:47,100
So, what does this one say?

103
00:05:47,860 --> 00:05:50,160
It's a question about thermal expansion.

104
00:05:50,540 --> 00:05:53,540
Thermal expansion? Oh, man, that's kid stuff.

105
00:05:53,540 --> 00:06:00,300
To put it in terms you'll understand, most things expand when they get hot and contract when they get cold.

106
00:06:00,580 --> 00:06:01,900
Well, it sounds simple enough.

107
00:06:01,920 --> 00:06:06,880
Look, if I were to warm up my breasts with my hands, do you think they'd grow bigger or smaller?

108
00:06:06,880 --> 00:06:09,600
I don't know. I don't think about things like that.

109
00:06:09,800 --> 00:06:11,720
Such a boring little boy.

110
00:06:11,720 --> 00:06:34,820
Hey, Shinji! Looky, looky!

111
00:06:35,240 --> 00:06:37,240
Back-rolling, Three!

112
00:06:39,240 --> 00:06:39,780
Oh...

113
00:06:39,780 --> 00:06:53,020
This just isn't clear enough.

114
00:06:53,500 --> 00:06:58,340
But the report from the Mount Asuma Earthquake Research Lab implies we should take a closer look at this shadow.

115
00:06:58,540 --> 00:06:59,520
We can't ignore it.

116
00:07:00,140 --> 00:07:01,320
What do the Magi say?

117
00:07:01,940 --> 00:07:03,320
It's 50-50 odds.

118
00:07:03,820 --> 00:07:04,520
Who's up there?

119
00:07:05,120 --> 00:07:07,540
Captain Katsuragi has already arrived at the site.

120
00:07:09,780 --> 00:07:14,480
You're going, 2G.

121
00:07:14,540 --> 00:07:16,140
Pin the probe down another 500.

122
00:07:22,100 --> 00:07:23,340
Depth 1,200.

123
00:07:23,600 --> 00:07:25,520
The pressure-resistant partition is cracking.

124
00:07:26,160 --> 00:07:27,100
Katsuragi.

125
00:07:27,420 --> 00:07:29,080
If it breaks, we'll pay for the damage.

126
00:07:29,180 --> 00:07:30,100
200 more, please.

127
00:07:33,800 --> 00:07:35,280
We're monitoring a reaction.

128
00:07:37,340 --> 00:07:38,380
Start analysis.

129
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:39,520
Right.

130
00:07:39,780 --> 00:07:50,700
The probe is imploded due to the extreme pressure.

131
00:07:51,360 --> 00:07:51,960
Did you get it?

132
00:07:52,760 --> 00:07:53,560
Just barely.

133
00:07:54,220 --> 00:07:55,160
The pattern is blue.

134
00:07:55,740 --> 00:07:56,700
Then there's no doubt.

135
00:07:57,140 --> 00:07:57,820
It's an angel.

136
00:07:58,280 --> 00:08:01,300
This laboratory is now under the jurisdiction of NERV.

137
00:08:01,420 --> 00:08:03,300
There will be no unauthorized phone calls.

138
00:08:03,300 --> 00:08:09,660
Any access to the outside world is prohibited, and all records pertaining to these events will be classified top secret.

139
00:08:11,300 --> 00:08:12,100
Katsuragi here.

140
00:08:12,220 --> 00:08:14,220
I need an A-17 from Commander Ikari.

141
00:08:14,220 --> 00:08:15,020
Top priority.

142
00:08:15,020 --> 00:08:16,740
Watch what you're saying, Captain.

143
00:08:16,940 --> 00:08:18,700
This isn't a secure line.

144
00:08:18,700 --> 00:08:19,700
I know that.

145
00:08:20,060 --> 00:08:22,200
Switch me to a scramble line immediately.

146
00:08:23,200 --> 00:08:26,120
At A-17, you want to make an offensive attack?

147
00:08:26,120 --> 00:08:27,260
That is correct.

148
00:08:27,460 --> 00:08:27,740
No.

149
00:08:28,160 --> 00:08:29,280
It's too dangerous.

150
00:08:29,780 --> 00:08:31,960
Have you forgotten what happened 15 years ago?

151
00:08:32,380 --> 00:08:33,820
No, but consider this.

152
00:08:34,080 --> 00:08:38,440
This is our chance to move from a state of perpetual defense to an offensive posture.

153
00:08:38,440 --> 00:08:40,360
The risk would be enormous.

154
00:08:40,940 --> 00:08:46,780
However, I'm sure that you must be aware of how important it is to obtain a living angel as a sample, am I correct?

155
00:08:47,200 --> 00:08:49,020
We will not tolerate failure.

156
00:08:50,400 --> 00:08:50,920
Failure.

157
00:08:51,520 --> 00:08:55,340
If we fail, it will result in the extinction of the entire human race.

158
00:08:56,340 --> 00:08:58,040
Are you really going to do it, Commander?

159
00:09:00,280 --> 00:09:01,460
Is that an angel?

160
00:09:01,780 --> 00:09:02,140
Yes.

161
00:09:02,240 --> 00:09:06,000
It's some sort of chrysalis form that precedes the adult stage we're familiar with.

162
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:09,020
This operation's prime objective will be to capture this angel.

163
00:09:09,300 --> 00:09:13,260
We must capture it alive and in a form as close to its original state as possible.

164
00:09:13,520 --> 00:09:14,520
And if we fail?

165
00:09:14,640 --> 00:09:16,120
Then you must destroy it immediately.

166
00:09:16,440 --> 00:09:16,820
Understood?

167
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:17,500
Roger!

168
00:09:17,620 --> 00:09:19,240
The designated pilot will be...

169
00:09:19,240 --> 00:09:19,940
Oh, pick me, please!

170
00:09:20,040 --> 00:09:21,000
I love to go diving!

171
00:09:21,640 --> 00:09:23,980
It's going to be me, as always.

172
00:09:24,360 --> 00:09:24,720
Asuka.

173
00:09:25,120 --> 00:09:25,380
Huh?

174
00:09:25,780 --> 00:09:27,200
You will carry out the mission.

175
00:09:27,720 --> 00:09:28,220
Sure!

176
00:09:28,960 --> 00:09:30,200
It's gonna be easy!

177
00:09:30,960 --> 00:09:31,760
And me?

178
00:09:31,940 --> 00:09:35,680
The special equipment we'll be using hasn't been standardized for use in the prototype.

179
00:09:36,000 --> 00:09:39,160
Ray and Unit Zero will remain here on standby.

180
00:09:39,420 --> 00:09:39,920
I see.

181
00:09:40,420 --> 00:09:41,940
Oh, poor little Ray.

182
00:09:42,160 --> 00:09:43,960
She doesn't get to have any fun!

183
00:09:44,680 --> 00:09:48,300
Now that an A-17 has been ordered, we've got to roll out immediately.

184
00:09:48,640 --> 00:09:49,100
Get ready.

185
00:09:49,500 --> 00:09:49,760
Roger!

186
00:09:52,240 --> 00:09:52,800
Huh?

187
00:09:53,020 --> 00:09:57,380
You know, this heat-resistant entry-plug suit doesn't seem any different from our regular ones.

188
00:09:57,900 --> 00:09:59,680
Press the switch on your right wrist.

189
00:09:59,800 --> 00:10:00,100
Okay!

190
00:10:00,820 --> 00:10:01,120
Oh!

191
00:10:01,840 --> 00:10:02,180
What?

192
00:10:02,960 --> 00:10:04,700
They brought the nails!

193
00:10:04,700 --> 00:10:07,940
Unit 2 should be ready now.

194
00:10:08,760 --> 00:10:09,260
No!

195
00:10:09,920 --> 00:10:10,920
No way!

196
00:10:11,060 --> 00:10:12,020
How could you?

197
00:10:12,220 --> 00:10:14,360
This exosuit is designed to protect you.

198
00:10:14,560 --> 00:10:18,620
Type D equipment is for combat under extreme environmental duress, not high fashion.

199
00:10:18,900 --> 00:10:20,340
That my Unit 2?

200
00:10:20,780 --> 00:10:22,160
The poor thing!

201
00:10:22,740 --> 00:10:23,580
Forget it!

202
00:10:23,860 --> 00:10:24,800
I won't do it!

203
00:10:25,120 --> 00:10:27,360
I'm not appearing in public in this stupid thing!

204
00:10:27,360 --> 00:10:29,720
This is the sort of thing you have Shinji for!

205
00:10:29,920 --> 00:10:31,520
I'm so disappointed!

206
00:10:31,520 --> 00:10:35,040
I was looking forward to seeing you in action!

207
00:10:35,300 --> 00:10:37,140
He's there behind Opa-loopa!

208
00:10:37,900 --> 00:10:42,240
Dr. Akagi, I just can't let Paji see me in this awful-looking thing!

209
00:10:42,620 --> 00:10:44,060
Are we having problems down there?

210
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:45,420
Sort of, yes.

211
00:10:45,700 --> 00:10:47,340
Excuse me, but I could...

212
00:10:47,340 --> 00:10:48,880
I will go in Unit 2.

213
00:10:49,300 --> 00:10:49,600
Ah!

214
00:10:51,260 --> 00:10:52,640
Oh, no, you don't!

215
00:10:52,760 --> 00:10:55,760
The only way you're using my Unit 2 is over my dead body!

216
00:10:56,040 --> 00:10:58,480
I'd rather do it than let her take my place!

217
00:11:01,120 --> 00:11:02,460
I'm sorry, Liebkin.

218
00:11:02,460 --> 00:11:03,780
They made me do it!

219
00:11:03,780 --> 00:11:19,160
Ava Units 1 and 2 have arrived.

220
00:11:20,200 --> 00:11:21,820
Have both units stand by.

221
00:11:22,260 --> 00:11:25,140
Reposition the laser bore and stand ready on the crane.

222
00:11:25,420 --> 00:11:25,700
Roger.

223
00:11:29,420 --> 00:11:31,680
Hey, is Kaji here yet?

224
00:11:31,680 --> 00:11:33,620
God's gift won't be coming.

225
00:11:33,740 --> 00:11:34,980
He's got no business here.

226
00:11:35,420 --> 00:11:39,200
No, but I wanted him to see me in my greatest triumph to date!

227
00:11:40,620 --> 00:11:42,440
An A-17 has been ordered.

228
00:11:42,660 --> 00:11:44,340
This will include a freeze of all assets.

229
00:11:44,720 --> 00:11:47,000
So that means that some people will be in trouble.

230
00:11:47,500 --> 00:11:48,860
Why didn't you try to stop them?

231
00:11:49,100 --> 00:11:50,740
I had no way of stopping this.

232
00:11:50,920 --> 00:11:52,880
This order was an official one, you know.

233
00:11:53,240 --> 00:11:55,340
But you must know that if Nerv fails at this,

234
00:11:55,420 --> 00:11:56,700
the entire world will perish.

235
00:11:57,100 --> 00:11:57,760
Don't worry.

236
00:11:57,760 --> 00:11:59,560
Not even they are that arrogant.

237
00:12:01,680 --> 00:12:04,320
What are those jets?

238
00:12:04,540 --> 00:12:07,000
The UN and the Air Force will be standing by.

239
00:12:07,380 --> 00:12:08,800
Until this mission's over anyway.

240
00:12:09,400 --> 00:12:10,660
Are they here to help us?

241
00:12:10,760 --> 00:12:13,120
No, they're here to clean up the mess.

242
00:12:13,480 --> 00:12:14,680
Just in case we fail.

243
00:12:15,180 --> 00:12:16,680
Uh, what do you mean?

244
00:12:16,920 --> 00:12:19,560
They'll use N2 depth charges to destroy the Angel.

245
00:12:19,840 --> 00:12:20,900
And us as well.

246
00:12:21,080 --> 00:12:22,380
This job sucks!

247
00:12:22,500 --> 00:12:24,760
What kind of a jerk would order something like that?

248
00:12:24,860 --> 00:12:25,820
Commander Ikari.

249
00:12:25,820 --> 00:12:26,300
Huh?

250
00:12:26,300 --> 00:12:34,160
Laser operation complete.

251
00:12:34,540 --> 00:12:35,960
The board path has been secured.

252
00:12:36,220 --> 00:12:37,920
The Type-D equipment is functioning normally.

253
00:12:38,600 --> 00:12:40,360
Unit 2 is ready and in position.

254
00:12:40,840 --> 00:12:41,300
Understood.

255
00:12:42,100 --> 00:12:43,440
Asuka, are you ready?

256
00:12:44,080 --> 00:12:44,980
Ready when you are.

257
00:12:45,340 --> 00:12:46,340
Let's do it!

258
00:12:46,340 --> 00:13:03,200
Unit 2 is entering the lava.

259
00:13:03,200 --> 00:13:05,360
Hey, look at this, Chi-Chi!

260
00:13:05,740 --> 00:13:08,320
A perfect dinner sign!

261
00:13:08,320 --> 00:13:17,100
Current depth, 170.

262
00:13:17,440 --> 00:13:19,240
Rate of descent, 20.

263
00:13:19,620 --> 00:13:20,860
No problems detected.

264
00:13:21,340 --> 00:13:22,520
Visibility is zero.

265
